<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Frederick, Grand Duke of Baden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1728–1811</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Frederick of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> ruled for 73 years, first as Margrave of Baden-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durlach">Durlach</a> from 1738. In 1771 he inherited Baden-Baden and reunited the margraviate. An enlightened ruler, he abolished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">serfdom</a> in 1783. Siding with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, he gained large territories and became Elector in 1803 and Grand Duke in 1806, making Baden a major state of south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-frederick-grand-duke-of-baden.jpg" alt="Charles Frederick, Grand Duke of Baden" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karl_Friedrich_Markgraf_von_Baden.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
